   "subject": "Change colour scale in stat_contour()",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I&#39;m having difficulty changing the color scale to anything but the default &#39;blues&#39; for contour plots with geom = &quot;polygon&quot;. I&#39;ve tried scale_fill_gradient(), etc. with no success. I&#39;m sure it&#39;s simple, but I&#39;m stuck. Code and example plot below. Data attached.</div><div>Thanks,<br>Kevin</div><div><br></div><div>load(interp_out.Rdata)</div><div><div>v &lt;- ggplot(interp.out, aes(x, y, z = z))</div><div><br></div><div>v + stat_contour(geom=&quot;polygon&quot;, aes(fill=..level..),binwidth=2) + stat_contour(binwidth=2) + facet_wrap(~freq) + </div><div>  scale_x_continuous(&#39;\\nAthwartship Beam Angle (deg)&#39;) + scale_y_continuous(&#39;Alongship Beam Angle (deg)\\n&#39;) +</div><div>  theme_bw()</div></div><div><br></div><div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/attach/24c61c2abf821659/image.png?part=0.0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"Inline image 1\" width=\"412\" height=\"363\"><br></div>\r\n</div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "5_VOPj9QKk0J",
   "from": "Brandon Hurr",
   "author": "27405c4b711a1080",
   "date": "2014-09-27T14:02:04Z",
